---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Dark Matter Candidates Cheat Sheet | Free WIMPs, Axions, Sterile Neutrinos"
  description="Complete dark matter candidates cheat sheet with WIMPs, axions, and sterile neutrinos. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Dark Matter Candidates<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>WIMPs, axions, and sterile neutrinos. From particle physics to cosmology.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>WIMPs</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Mass: ~ 10-1000 GeV/c²
Interaction: weak force
Detection: nuclear recoils
Cross section: σ ~ 10⁻⁴⁶ cm²
Status: no detection yet</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Experiments</h3>
        <pre><code>XENON1T/XENONnT: liquid xenon
LUX/LZ: liquid xenon
PandaX: liquid xenon
SuperCDMS: cryogenic germanium
DAMA/LIBRA: annual modulation claim</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Axions</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Mass: ~ 10⁻⁵-10⁻³ eV/c²
Interaction: very weak (strong CP problem)
Detection: conversion to photons in B field
Experiments: ADMX, HAYSTAC
Status: no detection yet</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Sterile Neutrinos</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Mass: keV range
Interaction: only gravity
Detection: X-ray decay line (3.5 keV?)
Experiments: XMM-Newton, Chandra
Status: unconfirmed signal</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Other Candidates</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Alternative Models</h3>
        <pre><code>MACHOs: brown dwarfs, black holes (ruled out)
Primordial black holes: varying mass range
Fuzzy dark matter: ultralight scalar field
Self-interacting dark matter:SIDM
Modified gravity: MOND (alternative to DM)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
